[ ] Build a WASM binding host over vault-style delivery $A browser/editor host supplies inventories and snapshots, executes the same EffectBatch against a vault API, and reuses Core codecs with zero format logic outside Core. Represent weaker atomicity, conflict, and partial failure honestly.$ !3 +wasm ^2026-08-20T09:41 #01a0200c-94ed-7152-acb3-1e173fedda40
[ ] Merge workspace-fs and cli into one effectful runtime crate, one binary $DECIDED 2026-09-18 with the user. Two crates: clearhead-core stays pure and separate (the WASM constraint is the only load-bearing boundary), and one effectful crate absorbs clearhead-workspace-fs plus the CLI commands, sparql and dataset, shipping the single clearhead binary. workspace-fs was only split out to serve multiple binaries. Orthogonality is kept as one-directional module dependencies and pub(crate) visibility, not crate count, with a small test that checks frontends never import each other. This removes the bin-private mod commands blocker at the root. Unblocks the mcp-scaffold action: clearhead mcp becomes a subcommand behind an mcp feature that implies sparql, with build/run split so nothing but the protocol writes to stdout. The LSP folds into the same binary later as its own action, since it carries a migration for the nvim plugin and an unsaved-buffer versus on-disk question for sparql. Not decided: how an id-less charter is represented without a clock in core.$ !2 ^2026-09-18T10:51 #01a0b5a4-ec3f-76ad-a63a-ca655a83364c
[ ] Fold the LSP into the single clearhead binary as a subcommand $Follows the merge into one effectful crate. clearhead lsp becomes a subcommand of the one binary, so the LSP can share the runtime and sparql. Costs to plan for: the nvim plugin and any installed setups must change their LSP cmd, and sparql reads the dataset from disk, so a query answered inside the LSP sees saved files rather than unsaved buffers. Decide whether that is acceptable or whether LSP-side queries are limited to cases where it does not matter. Not urgent and nothing blocks on it.$ !5 ^2026-09-18T11:03 #01a0b5b0-17df-74a1-ba34-bd9d04ac34a7
